GIT HUB Access token in JENKINS 

github-access-token Jenkins credentials ID hai — isko manually Jenkins mein add karna padta hai.

Yahan se step-by-step bata raha hoon:
✅ Step-by-Step: How to Add github-access-token to Jenkins
🔹 Step 1: Go to Jenkins Credentials

    Open Jenkins dashboard

    Click “Manage Jenkins”

    Click “Credentials”

    Under “(global)”, click → “Add credentials”

🔹 Step 2: Generate GitHub Token

    Go to: https://github.com/settings/tokens

    Click “Generate new token (classic)”

    Set:

        Note: Jenkins Deployment

        Expiration: Choose appropriate (e.g., 90 days or "No Expiry" if you're testing locally)

        Scopes (tick these):

            repo

            workflow (if CI/CD needed)

    Generate → Copy the token immediately

🔹 Step 3: Add Credential in Jenkins

    Back in Jenkins “Add Credentials” page:

        Kind: Username with password

        Username: git (or leave blank)

        Password: (Paste your GitHub token here)

        ID: github-access-token ✅

        Description: Something like "GitHub Token for Law Firm CRM"

Click Save ✅
🔹 Step 4: Use in Jenkinsfile

git branch: 'beta-master',
    url: 'https://github.com/Mhd-Hsyn/Law_Firm-CRM.git',
    credentialsId: 'github-access-token'

🎉 Result:

Jenkins ab securely GitHub se repo pull karega without exposing token in Jenkinsfile.

